
  Adding settings later is cheap. The storage key naming, the versioning of the stored blob, and whether identifiers are
  allowed in it are the parts that get expensive to change once data exists in real browsers.

  [1mMy recommendation: infrastructure + theme only.[0m It gets the persistence layer right without putting a user identifier
  into browser storage on day one, and "remember username" can be added deliberately later as its own decision.

